{
  "id": "Compound::DB01149 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Nefazodone is known to bind to Cyp3a7, a member of the cytochrome P450 family, and this binding is associated with the participation of Cyp3a7 in the metabolism of xenobiotics and aromatase activity. The evidence suggests that Nefazodone may indirectly influence Cyp3a4 through the activation of Cyp3a7, which in turn participates in the metabolism of substrates that are subsequently metabolized by Cyp3a4. This pathway implies a potential role for Nefazodone in modulating Cyp3a4 activity, though the direct interaction between Nefazodone and Cyp3a4 remains unconfirmed. The presence of multiple pathways linking Nefazodone to Cyp3a4 through Cyp3a7 highlights the complexity of the metabolic interactions, and further experimental validation would be necessary to establish a definitive mechanistic link.",
